            <ArticleTitle>[Early pulmonary changes caused by amiodarone].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>235-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Confluent infiltrates and interstitial condensates with (sub)segmentary spreading are typical radiological findings in amiodarone pneumopathy. A case is presented where daily amounts of 200-600 mg and a total of 18.3 g amiodarone led to alveolitis with fibrosis within 4 weeks, which is uncommon in the early stage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
